         <message name="IDS_CHROME_SIGNOUT_CONFIRMATION_PROMPT_VERIFY_BODY_WITH_COUNT" desc="This is the subtitle of an error message dialog that appears when the user opens the Chromium Profile Menu and chooses 'Sign out of Chromium'. The error message appears when the user has saved some data (like a password or payment method) to Chromium, but Chromium wasn't able to save the data to the user's Google Account due to a sign-in error; we want to set expectations by clarifying that the data will be removed from the device. This subtitle is after the 'Some data isn’t saved yet' string. The tone should be cautionary, because we want to explain to the user that their data is not saved and will be deleted if they sign out. This string provides a path to resolution because it explains how the user can properly save their data before they sign out of Chromium.">
